     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.CRISIS PREVENTION AND RECOVERY 

Trainings and ToT on Gender Based Violence Case Management

- 63 (23w) Police, Directorate of Combating Violence Against Women (DCVAW) and JCC employees trained on Gender and GBV, more importantly on dealing with survivors such as maintaining confidentiality and safeguarding the security of survivors.
-15 (6w) Police and DCVAW and JCC attended a ToT on gender and GBV with the aim to produce a pool of trainers who can train next generations of police officers on GBV and GBV case management. 

BASIC SERVICES 

- 7 water treatment plants project implemented in Basra. Five out of the seven projects were completed during 2021benefiting a population of 70,000 people within the catchment area. The projects have a total productivity capacity of 1,350m&#xb3;/hr averaging at 270m&#xb3;/hr.
-2 new water treatment plants projects were launched in 2021 and are steadily making progress. The two new projects will benefit around 782,000 residents of Al Alwaan area of Mdayna District and Al-Hussain neighborhood in Basra City with a productivity capacity of 800m&#xb3;/hr . 

LIVELIHOODS RECOVERY 
- 3,221 individuals benefited from business management training and SME grants. 
- 1,340 individuals benefited from business management training only.
- 13, 585 individuals benefited from short-term 40-days cash for work projects enabling access to immediate financial assistance (543,400 labour days).
- 1,008 individuals received vocational skills training in the high demand sectors.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
